From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fs/ntfs3: mark a new symlink absolute only for a full path on
 a drive

ntfs_create_reparse_buffer() takes any target whose second character is
':' for an absolute Windows path: it clears SYMLINK_FLAG_RELATIVE and
puts \??\ in front of the substitute name.  That includes "a:b" and
"C:x", which are not full paths.

Do this only for a drive letter, a ':' and a separator, as in C:/dir.
ntfs_reparse_set_native_symlink() in fs/ntfs makes the same test.

"ln -s C:data.txt l" used to store the substitute name \??\C:data.txt
without SYMLINK_FLAG_RELATIVE and now stores C:data.txt with it.  A
link to C:/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts is stored as before, and
Windows Server 2025 opens the file through it.

Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
---
 fs/ntfs3/inode.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ntfs3/inode.c b/fs/ntfs3/inode.c
index 2ce57f7..8552f18 100644
--- a/fs/ntfs3/inode.c
+++ b/fs/ntfs3/inode.c
@@ -1311,6 +1311,20 @@ static inline u32 ntfs_reparse_bytes(u32 uni_len, bool is_absolute)
 			SymbolicLinkReparseBuffer.PathBuffer);
 }
 
+/*
+ * ntfs_path_on_drive - Is this a full path on a drive, such as C:/dir?
+ *
+ * Windows always has a separator after the colon of a full path.  Without
+ * it the colon is just a character of a name, as far as Linux is
+ * concerned.
+ */
+static bool ntfs_path_on_drive(const char *path)
+{
+	return ((path[0] >= 'A' && path[0] <= 'Z') ||
+		(path[0] >= 'a' && path[0] <= 'z')) &&
+	       path[1] == ':' && (path[2] == '/' || path[2] == '\\');
+}
+
 static struct REPARSE_DATA_BUFFER *
 ntfs_create_reparse_buffer(struct ntfs_sb_info *sbi, const char *symname,
 			   u32 size, u16 *nsize)
@@ -1321,7 +1335,7 @@ ntfs_create_reparse_buffer(struct ntfs_sb_info *sbi, const char *symname,
 	typeof(rp->SymbolicLinkReparseBuffer) *rs;
 	bool is_absolute;
 
-	is_absolute = symname[0] && symname[1] == ':';
+	is_absolute = ntfs_path_on_drive(symname);
 
 	rp = kzalloc(ntfs_reparse_bytes(2 * size + 2, is_absolute), GFP_NOFS);
 	if (!rp)
